# Commit Documentation Hygiene

When work is ready to commit:

- Update the main documentation Markdown files so they reflect the code changes.
- Prefer editing existing docs such as `README.md` `CODEBASE_STRUCTURE.md` and `CODEBASE_DATAFLOW.md` ; do not create new documentation files unless the user asks.
- Remove obsolete documentation files or sections when they are clearly stale.
- Keep documentation concise. Keep the verbosity to low.
- Do not add any unnecessary comments or documentation. 
